## State Management
// Implementation of:
// - @code-style-and-structure.mdc#Performance-Guidelines#State-Management
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#Core-Requirements#State-Control

### Core State Principles
Single Source of Truth:
- Centralized state management
- Clear ownership of state updates
- Predictable state transitions
- Atomic state operations

Update Frequency:
- Global 1-second update timer
- Batch related state changes
- Optimize update scheduling
- Handle state dependencies

State Categories:
1. Battle State:
   - Phase tracking
   - Timer management
   - Victory conditions
   - Node ownership

2. Battalion State:
   - Position tracking
   - Health/status
   - Target information
   - Movement paths

3. Combat State:
   - Attack calculations
   - Damage resolution
   - Range checking
   - Collision detection

### State Updates
Update Process:
- Validate state changes
- Batch related updates
- Maintain consistency
- Handle edge cases

Error Handling:
- Validate state transitions
- Recover from failures
- Log state errors
- Maintain fallback states

### State Synchronization
Timing Requirements:
- Sync with global timer
- Handle network delays
- Manage animation states
- Coordinate multiple updates

Performance Optimization:
- Minimize state updates
- Batch similar changes
- Optimize calculations
- Monitor update frequency

Remember: Changes must directly support these core mechanics and maintain system integrity.

### Damage Calculation
// Implementation of:
// - @battle-node-control.mdc#Capture-System#Control-Progress
// - @battle-performance-standards.mdc#State-Updates#Combat-State

// Referenced by:
// - @battle-targeting-system.mdc#Combat-Sequence#Damage-Application
// - @battle-visual-feedback.mdc#Combat-Effects#Control-Feedback

Node Control Damage:
- Calculate total army health at battle start
- Set capture threshold at 75% of total health
- Track accumulated damage per side
- Apply damage immediately on hits
- Update control status after each hit

Battalion Combat:
- Calculate total attack power = base_offense * battalion_quantity
- Apply defense reduction: damage = attack * (1 - defense/100)
- Ensure minimum damage of 1 point
- Track individual battalion total health (base_health * quantity)
- Apply damage after defense calculation
- Trigger destruction at 0 total health

